From eca1f17a6f36526824f87506a2584fe8ab344e6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:03:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: read --use-system-ca certificates from OpenSSL below
 a 10.14 target

G5 nodejs22 build 2026-09-02, item #4 (src/crypto/crypto_context.cc):

  crypto_context.cc:492: error: 'kSecClass' was not declared in this scope
  ... kSecMatchLimit, kSecReturnRef, kSecClassCertificate,
      kSecMatchLimitAll, SecItemCopyMatching

The macOS branch of the system-CA store (ReadMacOSKeychainCertificates
and the trust-settings helpers it uses, ported from Chromium) is written
against the 10.14 SDK and runtime: SecItemCopyMatching,
SecCertificateCopyData and SecPolicyCreateSSL are 10.6 APIs,
SecPolicyCopyProperties 10.7, kSecPolicyAppleSSL 10.9,
SecTrustEvaluateWithError 10.14 - upstream builds with an 11.0
deployment target.  None of that exists on the PowerPC SDKs, and a
re-implementation on the 10.5 keychain API (SecKeychainSearch*,
SecCertificateGetData, SecTrustEvaluate) is not worth having for this
port.

Gate the block and its call on the deployment target the code needs:
NODE_USE_MACOS_KEYCHAIN_CA is defined when
__ENVIRONMENT_MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED__ >= 101400 (the compiler
always defines that macro on Darwin; no <AvailabilityMacros.h> needed).
Builds targeting 10.14 or later are unchanged.  Below that,
InitializeSystemStoreCertificates takes the same branch as the other
POSIX platforms, GetOpenSSLSystemCertificates: the SSL_CERT_FILE /
SSL_CERT_DIR environment variables, else OpenSSL's compiled-in
X509_get_default_cert_file() / _dir() - with MacPorts' openssl3 the
OPENSSLDIR it was configured with, which certsync/curl-ca-bundle
populate.  --use-system-ca stays opt-in as upstream.  The Security
framework include moves under the same macro.  TrustStatus (also used
by the Windows branch) stays where it is.

Sweep: this block is node's only user of post-10.5 Apple APIs (grep of
src/ for the Security, libdispatch, os_log, libproc, clonefile and
QoS/thread-policy families finds nothing else; the copyfile hits are
libuv's uv_fs_copyfile).
---
 src/crypto/crypto_context.cc | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/crypto/crypto_context.cc b/src/crypto/crypto_context.cc
index 8028f6d..df000b0 100644
--- a/src/crypto/crypto_context.cc
+++ b/src/crypto/crypto_context.cc
@@ -19,8 +19,17 @@
 #include <openssl/engine.h>
 #endif  // !OPENSSL_NO_ENGINE
 #ifdef __APPLE__
+// The keychain and trust-settings code below is written against the 10.14
+// SDK and runtime: SecItemCopyMatching, SecCertificateCopyData and
+// SecPolicyCreateSSL are 10.6, SecPolicyCopyProperties 10.7,
+// kSecPolicyAppleSSL 10.9, SecTrustEvaluateWithError 10.14.  With an older
+// deployment target (the PowerPC systems) --use-system-ca reads the OpenSSL
+// default certificate locations instead, like the other POSIX platforms.
+#if __ENVIRONMENT_MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED__ >= 101400
+#define NODE_USE_MACOS_KEYCHAIN_CA 1
 #include <Security/Security.h>
 #endif
+#endif
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <Windows.h>
@@ -304,7 +313,7 @@ bool isSelfIssued(X509* cert) {
 // Licensed under a BSD-style license
 // See https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/LICENSE for
 // details.
-#ifdef __APPLE__
+#ifdef NODE_USE_MACOS_KEYCHAIN_CA
 TrustStatus IsTrustDictionaryTrustedForPolicy(CFDictionaryRef trust_dict,
                                               bool is_self_issued) {
   // Trust settings may be scoped to a single application
@@ -547,7 +556,7 @@ void ReadMacOSKeychainCertificates(
   }
   CFRelease(curr_anchors);
 }
-#endif  // __APPLE__
+#endif  // NODE_USE_MACOS_KEYCHAIN_CA
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
 
@@ -815,13 +824,13 @@ static std::vector<X509*>& GetBundledRootCertificates() {
 
 static std::vector<X509*> InitializeSystemStoreCertificates() {
   std::vector<X509*> system_store_certs;
-#ifdef __APPLE__
+#ifdef NODE_USE_MACOS_KEYCHAIN_CA
   ReadMacOSKeychainCertificates(&system_store_certs);
 #endif
 #ifdef _WIN32
   ReadWindowsCertificates(&system_store_certs);
 #endif
-#if !defined(__APPLE__) && !defined(_WIN32)
+#if !defined(NODE_USE_MACOS_KEYCHAIN_CA) && !defined(_WIN32)
   GetOpenSSLSystemCertificates(&system_store_certs);
 #endif
   return system_store_certs;
-- 
2.43.0

